# Cloudflare Pages headers file (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# Everything in `public/` is copied verbatim into the build output, so this
# file ships as-is to Cloudflare Pages — no build step touches it.
#
# REQ-001 R-7.5 — baseline security response headers, on every production
# page response (AC1: X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, CSP; AC2: the
# CSP must not break any real page — see the derivation note below).
#
# Deliberately NOT included here: Strict-Transport-Security. That is R-7.4
# AC2, which belongs with the domain/TLS work (Wave 4, owner-blocked on
# E1/E2) — an HSTS header shipped before the zone/TLS setup is finished is
# far harder to safely undo than any header in this file, so it stays out
# until R-7.4 lands deliberately, not as a side effect of this change.
#
# CSP derivation (inspected the live production responses at
# https://haroonie-ai-public-site.pages.dev/ across every R-2 route — home,
# services, about, contact, privacy, terms, 404 — rather than guessing):
#   - No external scripts, stylesheets, fonts, images, or XHR/fetch targets
#     exist anywhere in the built output. Every page is self-hosted static
#     HTML/CSS from this one origin.
#   - The only <script> element is `application/ld+json` structured data on
#     the home page. CSP's script-src does not govern non-JS "data block"
#     script types (application/ld+json, application/json, importmap), so
#     it does not need `'unsafe-inline'` and stays locked to 'self'.
#   - The Contact page's "Book a time to talk" link is a plain, same-tab-
#     opening-in-new-tab <a href> to https://www.haroonie.ai/booking, not an
#     iframe/script embed — it needs no CSP allowance at all, it's a normal
#     top-level navigation.
#   - Astro inlines each page's scoped component CSS as a <style> element in
#     <head> (not `style="..."` attributes — none exist). A static
#     Cloudflare Pages _headers file can't mint a per-response nonce, and
#     hashing every inline style block would need regenerating on every
#     content/CSS change, so `style-src` carries 'unsafe-inline' as a
#     deliberate, scoped exception — inline CSS injection cannot execute
#     script, unlike `script-src 'unsafe-inline'`, which this policy does
#     not have.
#   - The contact form has no `action` and its submit button is disabled
#     (not wired up yet — R-3.1/Wave 5). `form-action 'self'` is set now on
#     the reasonable assumption the eventual handler is same-origin; revisit
#     this directive when Wave 5 wires up real submission.
#
# Revisit this file whenever new content adds a real third-party dependency
# (analytics, a booking *embed* rather than a link, a webfont host, etc.) —
# nothing here should be loosened speculatively ahead of that.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
